#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0424ac0-b370-5c08-84a3-dc6283867914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327831} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d602b6-97bd-5178-9019-37c790a3279e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327832} {:answer/id #uuid "0716c8cc-f27d-5d21-a821-4bab1b52c9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327833} {:answer/id #uuid "8e328b6c-bd62-550e-9c73-422107851a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327834} {:answer/id #uuid "f9421362-243c-59fb-9b14-776213f2e061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0716c8cc-f27d-5d21-a821-4bab1b52c9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327833} :answer-field/id #uuid "7889743d-327d-57bd-982e-9697f8fed55f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f285e4c4-1506-574b-a01b-1dbc6576701f" :question/math-academy-id "q-127888" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d8e3452-c58b-55e5-8bdc-0322a3571f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327838} {:answer/id #uuid "95f5313b-2533-5e2a-b56d-6e393be0efed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,5⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327839} {:answer/id #uuid "9ebc6caf-d4d9-52a1-b565-9a5fad41a2b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,3,1⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327840} {:answer/id #uuid "870342b4-fbe6-5d81-ad28-fd24046f8db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,1,1⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327841} {:answer/id #uuid "e03249e2-8b20-5e32-861e-e339f5fbd2ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,5,1⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d8e3452-c58b-55e5-8bdc-0322a3571f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327838} :answer-field/id #uuid "d81d19d4-cbc5-5cfe-b969-a0edb8b92b1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2be28e3f-f1b3-59f8-8a49-10d946563092" :question/math-academy-id "q-127936" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,5⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-3,0,2)$ and $B(2,1,3)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,1,3⟩-⟨-3,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨5,1,1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =⟨3,-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,1,1⟩ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c44dd24-9762-5b0f-b8c3-c517b9b60ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=⟨1,-4,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327845} {:answer/id #uuid "36d4f699-5e4c-578c-81de-dd6dc5597532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327846} {:answer/id #uuid "17782156-c5bc-52bc-b35a-443a7c32e894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327847} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f58c9a-fc06-5d06-ba42-d722b09b44a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327848} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef10d49-a269-52f1-b2ec-680de72f81b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=⟨-1,5,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36d4f699-5e4c-578c-81de-dd6dc5597532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327846} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05dd2c3-a082-50ce-aad1-f27b3c1cd170" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b72bbef8-b4f4-5c9e-9fbc-de2a30c271f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-33317" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-4,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,6,-4⟩-⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8774269b-3079-5838-8e20-b63286c329a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117607} {:answer/id #uuid "8c24e893-0b40-5d3f-a998-dcb0ba36e49d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117608} {:answer/id #uuid "1c742a2e-7c7b-58b7-bcc1-018a1b4c0473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117609} {:answer/id #uuid "7698e5e6-2811-503f-b463-d209ca3b1a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117610} {:answer/id #uuid "7a04dcae-4de5-5376-bea3-a84f508e95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a04dcae-4de5-5376-bea3-a84f508e95ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117611} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd8acfb-e547-539e-b562-9ee71ef61e78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d32af589-36a2-5da2-a4fd-d2edd8386949" :question/math-academy-id "q-33319" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84dc2945-12d3-5d21-a2b2-0e1b178a1f18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,3⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327852} {:answer/id #uuid "89b27076-6383-5826-9e77-b4544ff8773e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=⟨4,-2,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327853} {:answer/id #uuid "619108c5-9406-5b3d-a388-a20303cab86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327854} {:answer/id #uuid "b93e45ae-6875-5610-970d-6c3f3352e094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327855} {:answer/id #uuid "4e82c617-671f-5b80-a52e-7a40798816db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,3⟩=⟨2,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "619108c5-9406-5b3d-a388-a20303cab86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327854} :answer-field/id #uuid "c93285b5-44df-5ba9-b589-5b8105d8a3e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7c09730-9f8b-58d2-86e4-ff2f0b0d0e80" :question/math-academy-id "q-70893" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(4,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-1,0,1)$ and $B(1,0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨4,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-1,0,1)$ and $B(1,0,-1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,0,-1⟩-⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨2,0,-2⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
